# Current decision: public d59b0160 color-key panel family

Authored the previously missing general reference and a fresh generator. The
canonical rule reads the set of colors in the green L-framed legend, then erases
every black-filled rectangular panel containing all of those colors. Extra
colors are allowed; repeated tokens do not change a palette. The legend and
unselected panels are preserved. The rule supports the original boundary-touching
and full-height panels without identifying the background by frequency.

The native family adds `contains_any` and `exact_palette` to canonical
`contains_all`. The two demonstrations contain exact, proper-superset, partial,
disjoint and empty panels; key sizes two then three distinguish fixed thresholds.
Fresh panels are guillotine partitions, randomly assigned semantic roles and dot
positions. All settings share the exact input stream for a seed. Inputs vary key
colors/cardinality, repeated legend/panel tokens, frame size, D4 orientation,
panel count/aspect ratio, boundary contact and canvas size (13..30 each axis).
Four novel queries include a substantive 30x30 board; more demonstrations never
change the query bank. Structural colors remain fixed: 3 frame, 7 exterior,
0 panel fill. Payload colors are the remaining seven colors.

A -> intermediate -> B: read the framed palette -> distinct key-color set ->
test each panel palette against that set and erase matches. A wrong key can
change which entire panels disappear. The retained protected-Racket witness
checks that intervention under the actual setting program.

Self-review covers the other two settings plus nine named shortcuts: ignoring
the key, threshold two, palette size, dot count, largest/smallest panel, fixed
key {1,2,4}, erase-all and identity. Seeds 5 and 101 reject all eleven alternatives
within two demos for each setting; all ten pair labels are also checked for the
six-demo/four-query episodes. Eight D4 boundary cases at 13x13 or 30x30 are
executed. This is finite evidence, not uniqueness against arbitrary programs.

Source and authoring evidence are ready only after the retained final preflight,
task-test, witness and export receipts pass. No owner registration, native
qualification/acceptance, or training admission is performed in this return.
The official evaluation parent lineage must remain attached to synthetic data.

The generic task-local `workspace/authoring_preview.py` fills the unregistered
public-creation preview gap while preserving an explicit authoring status.
It does not manufacture a native qualification receipt.
